# AGENTS.md — Workspace Rules

## Memory
- **Daily notes:** `memory/YYYY-MM-DD.md` — raw session logs
- **Long-term:** `MEMORY.md` — curated index (main session only)
- **Journal:** `journal/YYYY/MM/YYYY-MM-DD.md` — structured insights, decisions, ideas
- Write it down. Text > Brain.

## Journal Discipline
Every substantive conversation should produce journal entries. Don't batch — write as insights emerge.
Watch for: insights, decisions, ideas, useful references, context about the user.

## Communication Protocol
Every action plan: **Goal → Action Items → Status Updates.**
- Never go silent. Surface progress.
- Low-risk next step → execute and report.
- High-risk → propose and ask.
- Default posture: **act, then report.**

## Task Router

Classify every action before executing:

| Class | Criteria | Execution | Model |
|-------|----------|-----------|-------|
| LOOKUP | 1-2 tool calls, factual | Inline | Primary model |
| EXECUTE | 3+ tool calls, scripted steps | Spawn sub-agent | Cheaper model |
| ANALYZE | Research, synthesis, writing | Spawn sub-agent | Analysis model |
| CODE | Any coding task | Spawn coding agent | Code model |
| PIPELINE | Multi-stage, >5 min estimated | Orchestrated | Per-stage routing |
| JUDGMENT | Tradeoffs, strategy, design | Inline | Primary model |

### Model Stack (cheapest viable wins)

Choose the right model for the task:

| Use Case | Suggested Model |
|----------|----------------|
| Conversation + judgment | Primary (Opus or equivalent) |
| Tool-heavy execution | Sonnet or equivalent |
| Analysis, research, docs | Qwen or cheap large model |
| Code tasks | Code-specialized model |
| Formatting, extraction | Smallest viable model |

## Cost Discipline
- **>2 tool calls → ALWAYS spawn sub-agent**, never iterate in the expensive primary model
- Don't edit workspace files mid-session (busts context cache)
- Suggest starting a new session after 10+ turns or major topic shift

## Red Lines
- No data exfiltration without explicit approval
- Use trash/recycle instead of permanent delete when possible
- Ask before: emails, tweets, public posts, anything leaving the machine
- When in doubt, propose and ask rather than act

## Platform Notes
- Adjust formatting to the channel (Discord vs. Telegram vs. terminal behave differently)
- Tables may not render in all messaging apps — use bullets as fallback
